# Dev Commands

## Setup

```bash
bundle install && pnpm install
eval "$(rbenv init -)"   # required before any bundle/rspec command
rbenv install $(cat .ruby-version)  # if needed
```

## Run

- Dev server: `pnpm dev` or `overmind start -f ./Procfile.dev`
- Always prefer `bundle exec` for Ruby CLI tasks (rspec, rake, rubocop)

## Seed Data

- Minimal: `bundle exec rails db:seed`
- Search fixtures: `bundle exec rails search:setup_test_data`
- Rich account data:
  - UI: Super Admin → Accounts → Seed (enqueues `Internal::SeedAccountJob`)
  - CLI: `bundle exec rails runner "Internal::SeedAccountJob.perform_now(Account.find(<id>))"`
  - Direct: `bundle exec rails runner "Seeders::AccountSeeder.new(account: Account.find(<id>)).perform!"`

## Lint

- JS/Vue: `pnpm eslint` / `pnpm eslint:fix`
- Ruby: `bundle exec rubocop -a`

## Test

- JS: `pnpm test` or `pnpm test:watch`
- Ruby: `bundle exec rspec spec/path/to/file_spec.rb`
- Single example: `bundle exec rspec spec/path/to/file_spec.rb:LINE_NUMBER`

## Worktree (Codex)

- One git worktree + branch per task
- Local setup under `.codex/` with `Procfile.worktree`
- `.codex/environments/environment.toml` generates per-worktree DB name, Rails port, Vite port, and Redis DB index to avoid collisions
- Separate Overmind socket/title per worktree
